{"event_type":"review","id":"7ce0d9722cf5d7b9b1d1df359216dab0b5227d4478cbf8b07e0f20c9d13e9295","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T16:18:34Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/13f5a7a1a0a1b37f946a0e29bc9efd28eadf580b2fadfd3f650c5cf46d139eb1","sha256":"13f5a7a1a0a1b37f946a0e29bc9efd28eadf580b2fadfd3f650c5cf46d139eb1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7f9d5cf7b3a4638972ce04fae8d283f64c220fee7633818153b5c961d58e0794","sha256":"7f9d5cf7b3a4638972ce04fae8d283f64c220fee7633818153b5c961d58e0794"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1dfd5c462de853f03bf611463f41cfe6e91f07472afd76562e38c59920c35ea0","sha256":"1dfd5c462de853f03bf611463f41cfe6e91f07472afd76562e38c59920c35ea0"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4f666d01aaa9b05f054636ad248cd7a6d8e240906086e2788e9555df668b2e6a","sha256":"4f666d01aaa9b05f054636ad248cd7a6d8e240906086e2788e9555df668b2e6a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/64ed6f4683b6ea06682c5adc4fd2fdc032e666b4975db2e6b0778102bd82e748","sha256":"64ed6f4683b6ea06682c5adc4fd2fdc032e666b4975db2e6b0778102bd82e748"}],"attempt_id":"a2d6dff2d6fb807b39d552dba9c7418b43f31ed0390b3658db39b9813acbfb7c:0:1","base":"d0a48a237c26ed067b6ed720bd4ea3bc0f59a61d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"cddc74c39a77581474b6b23bb95e832c8be1e34d","body":"**Pair rewritten assertions across inserted non-assertion lines.**\n\n`expectationChangesOf` pairs each added line with the first queued removed line (`removed.shift()`, `src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts:125`). When an edit block inserts a non-assertion line before a rewritten assertion, that insertion consumes the removed line for the setup statement. The removed assertion is then consumed by the next non-assertion insertion. The re-added assertion finds an empty queue, so no `ExpectationChange` is recorded.\n\nFor example, replacing `const actual = oldValue();` and `expect(actual).toBe(1);` in `tests/example.test.ts` with `const actual = newValue();`, `const detail = actual.detail;`, and `expect(actual).toBe(2);` produces no observation. The `expect(...)` rewrite is a changed oracle, and the observer header requires such rewrites to be reported rather than passed silently (`src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts:1-14`, `16-24`).\n\nPair each re-added assertion-shaped line with the earliest unmatched removed assertion-shaped line in the same edit block, instead of only the next queued line. Keep the same-block boundary and the trimmed-difference check.","id":"03e77937868c2e25ff4023c4647bb5444b3133585550e61a26f3b8cc8328d780","intervals":[[125,125]],"path":"src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Pair rewritten assertions across inserted non-assertion lines."}],"head":"ef9d3f51c581dabb386d16d9d8e588d2cae60fd8","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"cddc74c39a77581474b6b23bb95e832c8be1e34d","intervals":[[1,155]],"path":"src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts"}],"job_id":"a2d6dff2d6fb807b39d552dba9c7418b43f31ed0390b3658db39b9813acbfb7c:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"cddc74c39a77581474b6b23bb95e832c8be1e34d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"cddc74c39a77581474b6b23bb95e832c8be1e34d","intervals":[[1,155]],"path":"src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"cddc74c39a77581474b6b23bb95e832c8be1e34d","intervals":[[1,155]],"path":"src/ops/gates/expectationChanges.ts"}],"scope_dig